direction: down
title: "UNWIND RESURRECTION NEEDS A REAL CLEAR\nFunction-body closure and actual caller closure are distinct"
title.shape: text
question: "Live trace saved U=1\nWhich admitted operation supplies U=0 before restore?"
normal: "Ordinary core domain: base depth h >= 1\nChecks clear only C; installers OR U\nNon-force resets see positive target depth\nOlder caller callbacks remain below nested root"
no: "Conditional invariant: U stays 1\nNo resurrection in this stated domain\nExcludes hooks, force/private writes, context switches"
private: "Supplied private entry at depth 0\nTclCheckExecutionTraces -> TraceExecutionProc\nCallback prefix begins with bracket substitution"
bracket: "Direct Tcl_EvalEx parses before command readiness\nBracket depth 0 -> 1; readiness rejects U\nBracket body is NOT executed"
clear: "Bracket restores depth 1 -> 0\nNon-force TclResetCancellation predicate is true\nU becomes 0; ERROR is retained"
revive: "Old trace whole-word restore\nSaved U=1 returns; traceCode still ERROR"
gap: "Private BODY path is closed\nNo existing zero-depth caller identified\nPrivate support / installed ABI / real client unresolved\nNot a reproduced Gambit or Tcl native bug"
question -> normal -> no
question -> private -> bracket -> clear -> revive -> gap
no.style.fill: "#E8F4E8"
clear.style.fill: "#DFEEFF"
gap.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
